{%- comment -%}
  The security and cache headers of Cloudflare Pages, written to /_headers. Like `redirects`, this
  source has no extension on purpose (Jekyll would add the source's extension to the permalink) and is
  listed in `exclude_from_localization`, so there is ONE file at the site root and none under /it/.
  The nginx fallback is deploy/nginx/headers.conf (the same policy, script/checks/csp.rb asserts it).

  CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY. Everything is 'self' except: the analytics script and its event endpoint
  (https://plausible.io, _data/site_meta.yml `analytics:`: another provider or script host must be added
  here and in headers.conf, the check says so), and the contact form, which POSTs to https://soshiki.io.
  There is no 'unsafe-inline' anywhere: the site has no inline style and no inline event handler. The ONE
  inline script (the no-js -> js switch in _includes/head.html) is allowed by its SHA-256 hash; the JSON-LD
  blocks (<script type="application/ld+json">) are data blocks, never executed, so the policy does not
  apply to them. Edit that script and the check fails with the new hash to paste here and in headers.conf.

  CLOUDFLARE MERGES the headers of every rule that matches a URL (the same header from two rules is
  joined with a comma), so the cache rules below never overlap: one rule per /assets/ folder.
  Fonts never change under their name: one year, immutable. Everything else under /assets/ is not
  fingerprinted (the file name stays when the content changes): an hour for the stylesheet and the scripts,
  a day for the pictures and the PDFs.

  *.pages.dev IS NEVER INDEXED. The two host rules at the end (Cloudflare Pages placeholders, a rule that
  starts with https://) answer only on the Pages hosts: the production alias (<project>.pages.dev) and
  the per-deployment URLs (<hash>.<project>.pages.dev). The custom domain is the only address that may
  be indexed. Previews (<branch>.<project>.pages.dev) are noindex by Cloudflare itself; the deploy job
  of .github/workflows/build.yml asserts the header on the URL it has just deployed.
{%- endcomment -%}
# Generated by the headers page (see the source in the repository). Do not edit.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-8lPAhsHw2YfhKzTADvM7cKkWnN0x+tW7bLY5CgC4aaY=' https://plausible.io; connect-src 'self' https://plausible.io; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; form-action 'self' https://soshiki.io; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/assets/team/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/assets/downloads/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
